.TH SQLITE-MANAGER 1 "August 2026" "sqlite-manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sqlite\-manager \- command-line shell for SQLite databases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sqlite\-manager
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I database
.RI [ sql ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sqlite\-manager
opens the SQLite database file
.I database
and either runs a single SQL command or starts an interactive shell.
.PP
If
.I sql
is given, it is executed and the program exits. Otherwise
.B sqlite\-manager
starts an interactive shell that reads SQL statements terminated by a
semicolon and prints query results as an aligned table.
.PP
Use the special name
.B :memory:
for a temporary in-memory database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information for the tool, the bundled library, and SQLite,
then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-readonly
Open the database in read-only mode; writes fail. The file must exist.
.TP
.B \-\-batch
Suppress interactive prompts. Useful when reading SQL from a pipe or file.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format for query results:
.B table
(default, a framed ASCII table),
.B csv
(RFC 4180 comma-separated values), or
.B json
(an array of one object per row).
.SH "INTERACTIVE SHELL"
Statements are accumulated until a terminating semicolon, then executed.
The following dot commands are recognized at the start of a statement:
.TP
.B .help
Show the list of dot commands.
.TP
.B .tables
List the tables in the database.
.TP
.BI .schema " [TABLE]"
Show the CREATE statements for every object, or just for
.IR TABLE .
.TP
.BI .read " FILE"
Execute the SQL statements contained in
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BR .quit ", " .exit
Leave the shell. End-of-input (Ctrl\-D) does the same.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A usage error occurred, the database could not be opened, or a statement
failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run one query and exit:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sqlite\-manager data.db "SELECT * FROM users"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a table in a new database:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sqlite\-manager data.db "CREATE TABLE t (id INTEGER, name TEXT)"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start an interactive shell on an in-memory database:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sqlite\-manager :memory:
.fi
.RE
.PP
Feed statements from a file in batch mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sqlite\-manager \-\-batch data.db < script.sql
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by VS.
